# The addon is the repository root, which is what the packager expects: it finds
# SimhammerInspector.toc beside .git and names the package after it.
#
# Everything listed here is development tooling that has no business in a zip a
# raider downloads. Folders beginning with a dot are dropped by the packager
# without being named, so .github and .git are not listed.
#
# README.md and LICENSE stay in: the packager turns the readme into the
# CurseForge description, and shipping the licence with the code is the point of
# having one.
ignore:
  - spec
  - tools
  - spike
  - docs
